  "planes_note": "Back to front: far (sky with the Milky Way, mountains, the pale cliff, the misty lake), forest, [the tank, enemies and props on the road], road, foreground. Each file is the reference's own 960 px cut plus its mirror (1920 px, seamless). y0 = the row of the 960x540 frame the plane's top sits on; parallax = scroll factor against the road (1.0). The tilt-shift blur is baked once by planes2.gd: blur_box_radius (two box passes); the reference already carries its own depth of field, so the far plane keeps it. darken = the factor baked into the foreground.",
  "zone_planes": {
    "note": "Free roam (docs/games/tank.md 2.10, 3.1): the zone's near plane replaces the forest plane (the same frame, y0, parallax and blur) while the tank drives through it; the pine forest keeps the forest plane. Built by zones.gd from the kit's own planes (the forest's trees squashed into lower tree lines, the far plane's pale cliff as quarry rock) plus houses, haystacks, fences, reeds and a gantry in code.",
